hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1136","Chapter mentioning what is taken without fighting, the fifth and select spoils, 1176 - Ibn al-Muqri' narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws, from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to spend on his family for a year from the wealth of Banu al-Nadir, which was of what Allah granted His Messenger of what the Muslims had not spurred horse or camel against. What remained he put into horses and weapons as equipment in the path of Allah."
"1137","1177 - Muhammad ibn Awf al-Ta'i narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Dinar, Abu al-Yaman and Bishr ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us; they said: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us that A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) informed him that Fatimah the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them) asking him for her inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in what Allah had granted His Messenger. Fatimah at that time was seeking the charity of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Medina and Fadak, and what remained of the fifth of Khaybar. A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited from; what we leave is charity. The family of Muhammad only eat from this wealth - meaning the wealth of Allah - they have no right to take more than their food. By Allah, I shall not change any of the charities of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the state they were in during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I shall act in them as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted."
"1138","1178 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi and Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us; they said: Waki' narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Khalid, from Abu al-Ala' Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, who said: We were sitting in al-Mirbad in Basra when a Bedouin came with a piece of leather or a scrap of a bag and said: This is a document the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for me. Abu al-Ala' said: I took it and read it to the people, and in it was: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is a document from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Banu Zuhayr ibn Uqaysh: If you establish prayer, give charity, and give from the spoils the fifth and the Prophet's share and the select portion, you are safe under Allah's covenant and the covenant of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say anything? He said: I heard him say: Fasting the month of patience, and fasting three days of every month, removes the rancour of the heart. He said: I said: Did you yourself hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Do you think I would lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Then he took the document and went off withdrawing. The hadith is that of al-Ahmasi, and the wording is close."
